  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Principal. The chairman of the board is Chief Mrs Solape Bayo, the accountant is Mr Jeremi Amos, and the counsellor is Mrs Beke Egbin.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    *The Lekki Headmaster*, a nickname earned over twenty-four years. *The Village Headmaster* is the television drama the nickname plays on.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Headmaster of Stardom Kiddies, the nursery and primary arm, before he rose to principal of the secondary school.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    She is the managing director, and the founder's daughter.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Chief Mrs Solape Bayo, who is also the managing director's mother. Gloss runs the school; her mother's board decides the money.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Her mother. The family relationship explains why the board's class anxiety and the management's decisions are so closely aligned.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    She is the vice principal, the one who keeps the assembly moving when Bepo cannot.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Justus Anabel, the chemistry teacher. The others are the fine-art teacher, the CRS teacher and the English teacher.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mrs Titi. Mrs Ladele is a parent, not a member of staff.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mrs Beke Egbin, who stays with Bepo after the assembly while the others return to their classes.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Ope Wande. Oyelana teaches CRS, which is a different thing from being the pastor the MD sends for.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Oyelana. The trap is Ope Wande, who is both a physics teacher and a pastor — the obvious wrong answer to this question.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Audu, whose jokes arrive at the moments the novel would otherwise become a sermon.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Fafore, who earns ₦175,000 a month, lives in Ifo and wakes at four to beat the traffic.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Jeremi Amos, who later drives Bepo to the airport with the others.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    A nurse. The teaching post in the United Kingdom is the one waiting for Bepo.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Nike and Kike, who live in the United Kingdom with their mother.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Egi Meko. Ogo is the parent at Fruitful Future, Guta the complaining parent at Stardom, and Oyelana a Stardom teacher.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Ogo, who withdraws his child when the offer is refused and is later arrested for murdering a client.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mrs Ignatius. Mrs Ladele is Bibi's mother, and the two parents are deliberately easy to confuse.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Guta, who is certain that *Ade as well as Jide comes early* is wrong and who is certain wrongly.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Banky and Tosh, whose quarrel runs from JSS3 into a lawsuit between their parents.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Chief Didi Ogba, detained for thirty-six months over ₦2.5 billion before being released and ordered to refund.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mrs Ladele. The teacher removed is Mr Ayesoro, the government teacher, whose tribal marks frightened the child.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Ayesoro, moved to another part of the group rather than sacked — a detail the paper likes because it is neither dismissal nor vindication.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Ogunwale. Oyelana and Amos travel separately to the airport, and Tai is the passport agent.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Tai. Sola, Jare and Hope are the migrants of Chapter 3, and Nku is the colleague who took a loan and disappeared.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Mr Nku. His story appears in Chapter 3 among the tales of how people fund a ticket.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Sola. Jare and Hope are the two cautionary tales told in the same chapter.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Powerful and unwilling to be corrected: the school's name stays wrong, the rite is served, and the school survives.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    She acts on the complaint and then laughs when she is corrected — the two halves of the same evidence.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Practical and impatient. The novel gives her the strongest material case in the book and no villainy at all.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Steady the school: she takes the assembly, and she addresses the students after he leaves. Comedy belongs to Audu and the board to Solape Bayo.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Egi Meko: the same job, the opposite choice — a school kept at the price of the man who keeps it.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Ten minutes produce nothing because the problem is a decision, not a grief. The novel uses the failure to raise the stakes.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    Each one carries a version of the argument: a family destroyed by migration, a career ended by a parent's certainty, a state that must be paid to work.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    An action, or a pattern of actions. A job title is a fact about employment, and what others say needs the same test as what the character does.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "D", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    If the scene would read exactly the same under the opposite trait, the trait is doing no work and the option is wrong.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    *Unwilling to be corrected* is a quality; the other three are offices a character holds.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "A", dense: true, pad: 5.47pt)[
    She complains about Mr Ayesoro, and the complaint ends his teaching career at Stardom — a parent's certainty doing what a rule should do.
  ]

]

